WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier,

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.940
And welcome to "Don't Escape 4...

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.160
.. Days...

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.720
.. I N   A   W A S T E L A N D"

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.180
If you remember "Don't Escape",

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.480
Er, if you don't remember "Don't Escape",

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.480
here is a synopsis of what it is.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.560
Uhhhhh...

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:14.860
You don't escape.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.720
There's been three other games before this,

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.500
It started out as a flash game that was tryna like,
reverse the concept of an escape room

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.320
Wha-- why am I giving you a history lesson? It doesn't matter.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.920
This is "Don't Escape 4", the games were amazing,

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.020
They're made by Scriptwelder, they're really cool.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.320
Let's do this!

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.880
Good. Glad we got that out of the way.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.580
Oh, also...

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.780
They're horror games.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.820
If I didn't mention that.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.720
You probably noticed because the whole intro sequence was so spooky.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.340
That doo- that door has got some issues on it.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.840
(READS ON-SCREEN TEXT)

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.400
Okay.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.320
(READS)

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.640
Now, you say "sturdy looking" door, I say...

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.100
.. shifting in and out of the plane of existence of reality that we're in."

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.960
A kinda like trans-dimensional door.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.240
What about the chimmneh?

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.460
(SEDUCTIVELY) Ohhh, yeah.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:00.260
Also, Scriptwelder has a really unique
pixelated style for their games. It's really cool.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.480
It's locked.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.340
Why am I not surprised?

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.480
Is that what I want though?

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:05.900
(WINDOW SMASHES)

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.900
OH! OH GOD!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.320
OH GOD NO!

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:11.920
No, wait, no...

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.380
Wait, was that bad?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.360
Was that good?

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.140
Oh. Oh okay. Alright.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.760
(READS)

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.000
Yeah, maybe it was the stinging, and laying eggs in my eyes.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.620
(READS)

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.880
Alright, well. Got my backpack.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.120
Uhhhh...

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.520
Move my head for a moment!

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.160
N I C E

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.780
So that's where my backpack is.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.380
But uh, I guess my head is gonna move to the other side of the screen,

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:42.420
in three!

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:43.520
Two!

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:44.560
One!

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.300
HUAGH- (EXPLOSION)

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:48.780
Ok, good. Now we're good.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:49.940
(READS)

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.460
That's not a good idea!

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.240
(DEEP VOICE) Oh-kay!

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.680
You got a story behind that,

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.880
or are you just gonna say that
the Moon's broken to pieces?

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.260
Okay, Mr. Depressing.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.700
Alright, thank you for that. That's real nice.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.860
I don't see nothin' else, so uh, guess here we go...

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.500
Run...

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.860
Yeah, you know what, you're right about that.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.700
(READS)

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.380
Oh yeah, wait. Hang on.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.960
You saying that you have powers of foresight?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.240
Journal. Ok, here we go.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.080
(READS)

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.840
Oh, the swarm, you say?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:13.880
Alright. Okay.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.520
I love this game already.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.920
I'm so into this.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.520
Love the setting, love everything about it. I'm down.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.840
I mean, I got nothing else to do,
so I might as well go for it.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.580
Well, good thing there is a nice human-sized hole.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.240
It's like Blues Clues!

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.100
